{"parentUuid":"7de656c9-4b59-47f6-9825-1d3416b07492","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0ccb5a8e-07a7-4d5f-8dbf-bda148be7f5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H9kbPu3Eb4z9HnHm3y4EcQ","type":"tool_result","content":"44\t\n45\tTo reduce over-redaction, Entire preserves structural transcript fields such as IDs and paths, ignores common placeholder values, and redacts only credential values for bounded key/value forms. When a connection string contains a real (non-placeholder) password, it is redacted as a unit because partial fragments can still expose sensitive material; connection strings whose passwords are placeholders (e.g. `${DB_PASSWORD}`) are left intact.\n46\t\n47\t## Customizing redaction\n48\t\n49\tThe built-in detectors handle well-known secret formats. For internal credential shapes that aren't covered (custom env-var prefixes, internal service tokens, project-specific session formats), Entire offers two extension surfaces. Both feed the same engine and run as their own layer between connection-string detection and bounded credential KV detection.\n50\t\n51\t### Surface 1: Inline `redaction.custom_secrets`\n52\t\n53\tAdd a label → regex map under `redaction.custom_secrets` in `.entire/settings.json`:\n54\t\n55\t```json\n56\t{\n57\t  \"redaction\": {\n58\t    \"custom_secrets\": {\n59\t      \"acme_token\":  \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\",\n60\t      \"internal_id\": \"INTERNAL_[a-z]{6}_[0-9]{4}\"\n61\t    }\n62\t  }\n63\t}\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t- The label is for diagnostics only; matches are replaced with the bare `REDACTED` token (matching the built-in secret layers, not the `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]` token used for PII).\n67\t- Regexes follow [Go's RE2 syntax](https://pkg.go.dev/regexp/syntax). No lookarounds, no backreferences.\n68\t- A failed compile is logged once at startup and the rule is skipped — it will never crash the redactor.\n69\t- Override in `.entire/settings.local.json` for personal additions; entries merge per-key (override replaces the same key, leaves other keys intact).\n70\t\n71\t### Surface 2: Rule packs\n72\t\n73\tDrop a YAML or JSON file into `.entire/redactors/`:\n74\t\n75\t```yaml\n76\t# .entire/redactors/acme-internal.yaml\n77\tname: acme-internal              # MUST match the filename stem\n78\tversion: 1.0.0\n79\tdescription: Internal ACME service tokens\n80\trules:\n81\t  - id: acme-token\n82\t    description: Long-lived ACME service tokens\n83\t    regex: 'ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}'\n84\t    samples:\n85\t      - { input: \"REDACTED\", redacted: true  }\n86\t      - { input: \"ACME_TOKEN_short\",                     redacted: false }\n87\t  - id: acme-session\n88\t    regex: 'asess_[a-f0-9]{32}'\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\tEquivalent JSON form:\n92\t\n93\t```json\n94\t{\n95\t  \"name\": \"acme-internal\",\n96\t  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n97\t  \"rules\": [\n98\t    {\n99\t      \"id\": \"acme-token\",\n100\t      \"regex\": \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\",\n101\t      \"samples\": [\n102\t        { \"input\": \"REDACTED\", \"redacted\": true  },\n103\t        { \"input\": \"ACME_TOKEN_short\",                     \"redacted\": false }\n104\t      ]\n105\t    }\n106\t  ]\n107\t}\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\t**Required fields:** `name` (must equal the filename stem — `acme-internal.yaml` → `acme-internal`), `version` (any string; semver recommended), and `rules[]` (at least one entry, each with `id` and `regex`).\n111\t\n112\t**Optional fields:** `description` (pack-level and rule-level), and `rules[].samples[]` (see \"Self-tests\" below).\n113\t\n114\t### Self-tests via `samples[]`\n115\t\n116\tEach rule may declare an array of `{input, redacted}` pairs. On the next process startup after editing the pack, Entire runs each sample and emits a `slog.Warn` for any mismatch:\n117\t\n118\t```\n119\tWARN  redactor pack sample mismatch  pack=.entire/redactors/acme-internal.yaml\n120\t      rule=acme-token sample_index=0 sample_length=42 expected=true got=false\n121\t```\n122\t\n123\tA failing sample never disables the rule — sample validation is informational. Use it to catch typos and false positives before they ship.\n124\t\n125\t### Distribution\n126\t\n127\t- **Within a team:** commit `.entire/settings.json` and/or `.entire/redactors/*` to your repo. Teammates pull and the rules apply.\n128\t- **Across teams:** copy the pack file or share a link to a gist; recipients drop the file into their `.entire/redactors/`.\n129\t- **Personal-only:** put the file in `.entire/redactors/local/` — `entire enable` writes that path into `.entire/.gitignore` so personal rules don't pollute team commits.\n130\t\n131\t### When to write a rule vs. file an issue\n132\t\n133\tWrite a rule for internal service tokens (`ACME_*`, `INTERNAL_*`), custom env-var prefixes the bundled detectors don't know about, and project-specific session formats.\n134\t\n135\tFile an issue when the rule would benefit every Entire user (e.g., a major SaaS issued a new token format), when a built-in is producing false positives on common idioms in your codebase, or when a built-in is *not* catching a well-known shared format (we'd rather fix the built-in than have everyone ship the same custom rule).\n136\t\n137\t### Troubleshooting\n138\t\n139\t- **My rule doesn't redact anything.** Warnings about invalid patterns or sample mismatches appear on stderr when Entire initializes redaction, such as hooks that write checkpoints or `entire doctor`. Look for lines mentioning your label or pack path.\n140\t- **My pack file is silently ignored.** Filenames must end in `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.json`. Other extensions are skipped.\n141\t- **I want to disable a rule temporarily.** Comment it out (prefix the YAML key with `#`) or remove the entry from `custom_secrets`. The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation.\n142\t\n143\t## Limitations"}]},"uuid":"b5d72e69-e5d4-4cd4-863f-0daff7fcfa6a","timestamp":"2026-05-01T20:01:07.002Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/security-and-privacy.md","content":"\nTo reduce over-redaction, Entire preserves structural transcript fields such as IDs and paths, ignores common placeholder values, and redacts only credential values for bounded key/value forms. When a connection string contains a real (non-placeholder) password, it is redacted as a unit because partial fragments can still expose sensitive material; connection strings whose passwords are placeholders (e.g. `${DB_PASSWORD}`) are left intact.\n\n## Customizing redaction\n\nThe built-in detectors handle well-known secret formats. For internal credential shapes that aren't covered (custom env-var prefixes, internal service tokens, project-specific session formats), Entire offers two extension surfaces. Both feed the same engine and run as their own layer between connection-string detection and bounded credential KV detection.\n\n### Surface 1: Inline `redaction.custom_secrets`\n\nAdd a label → regex map under `redaction.custom_secrets` in `.entire/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"custom_secrets\": {\n      \"acme_token\":  \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\",\n      \"internal_id\": \"INTERNAL_[a-z]{6}_[0-9]{4}\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- The label is for diagnostics only; matches are replaced with the bare `REDACTED` token (matching the built-in secret layers, not the `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]` token used for PII).\n- Regexes follow [Go's RE2 syntax](https://pkg.go.dev/regexp/syntax). No lookarounds, no backreferences.\n- A failed compile is logged once at startup and the rule is skipped — it will never crash the redactor.\n- Override in `.entire/settings.local.json` for personal additions; entries merge per-key (override replaces the same key, leaves other keys intact).\n\n### Surface 2: Rule packs\n\nDrop a YAML or JSON file into `.entire/redactors/`:\n\n```yaml\n# .entire/redactors/acme-internal.yaml\nname: acme-internal              # MUST match the filename stem\nversion: 1.0.0\ndescription: Internal ACME service tokens\nrules:\n  - id: acme-token\n    description: Long-lived ACME service tokens\n    regex: 'ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}'\n    samples:\n      - { input: \"REDACTED\", redacted: true  }\n      - { input: \"ACME_TOKEN_short\",                     redacted: false }\n  - id: acme-session\n    regex: 'asess_[a-f0-9]{32}'\n```\n\nEquivalent JSON form:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"acme-internal\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"rules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"acme-token\",\n      \"regex\": \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\",\n      \"samples\": [\n        { \"input\": \"REDACTED\", \"redacted\": true  },\n        { \"input\": \"ACME_TOKEN_short\",                     \"redacted\": false }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Required fields:** `name` (must equal the filename stem — `acme-internal.yaml` → `acme-internal`), `version` (any string; semver recommended), and `rules[]` (at least one entry, each with `id` and `regex`).\n\n**Optional fields:** `description` (pack-level and rule-level), and `rules[].samples[]` (see \"Self-tests\" below).\n\n### Self-tests via `samples[]`\n\nEach rule may declare an array of `{input, redacted}` pairs. On the next process startup after editing the pack, Entire runs each sample and emits a `slog.Warn` for any mismatch:\n\n```\nWARN  redactor pack sample mismatch  pack=.entire/redactors/acme-internal.yaml\n      rule=acme-token sample_index=0 sample_length=42 expected=true got=false\n```\n\nA failing sample never disables the rule — sample validation is informational. Use it to catch typos and false positives before they ship.\n\n### Distribution\n\n- **Within a team:** commit `.entire/settings.json` and/or `.entire/redactors/*` to your repo. Teammates pull and the rules apply.\n- **Across teams:** copy the pack file or share a link to a gist; recipients drop the file into their `.entire/redactors/`.\n- **Personal-only:** put the file in `.entire/redactors/local/` — `en